IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s391-fees`
IMPORT `dg11-s390-transfer-out`

-- Tests of dg11-s390-transfer-out.l4 (section 390). Expected values are worked by hand from the text of the section and written beside each assertion.

§ `Section 390(a) - who may move out`

-- (a)(1): only a jurisdiction outside the United States is a "foreign jurisdiction" here.
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `this State`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `another jurisdiction of the United States`
#ASSERT `s 390(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 390(a)(2) the entity is the resulting entity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a)(2) the entity is the resulting entity` FALSE
-- (a): a Delaware corporation, a foreign jurisdiction, and the five steps done.
#ASSERT `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` TRUE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` FALSE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` TRUE `another jurisdiction of the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` TRUE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` TRUE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` TRUE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- the election to continue picks the certificate
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the certificate that the corporation files` TRUE EQUALS `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the certificate that the corporation files` FALSE EQUALS `a certificate of transfer`

§ `Section 390(b) - the resolution`

-- The resolution, by position: adopted by the board; specifies the foreign jurisdiction; states that the Delaware existence is to continue; recommends approval by the stockholders; plan approved together.
`a complete resolution` MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a resolution not adopted` MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a resolution that names no jurisdiction` MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a resolution that omits the statement of continued existence` MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a resolution that does not recommend` MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a resolution with the plan not approved together` MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Arguments: the resolution; the corporation elects to continue?; a plan is to be adopted?
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a complete resolution` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution not adopted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution that names no jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE
-- the statement of continued existence is needed only "if applicable", that is when the corporation elects to continue
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution that omits the statement of continued existence` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution that omits the statement of continued existence` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution that does not recommend` TRUE TRUE
-- the plan is approved together with the resolution only "if a plan ... is to be adopted"
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution with the plan not approved together` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` `a resolution with the plan not approved together` TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 390(b) - the meeting and its notice`

-- A meeting on 30 June 2026. "At least 20 days prior": notice on 10 June (exactly 20 days) is in time, 11 June (19 days) is not, 9 June (21 days) is.
-- By position: an annual or special meeting; states time, place and purpose; given to each holder, voting or nonvoting, at the address on the records; date given; date of the meeting.
`notice given 20 days before` MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YearMonthDay 2026 6 10, YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
`notice given 19 days before` MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YearMonthDay 2026 6 11, YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
`notice given 21 days before` MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YearMonthDay 2026 6 9, YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
`notice that omits the purpose` MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, YearMonthDay 2026 6 9, YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
`notice sent only to the voting holders` MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 6 9, YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
`notice of a meeting that is neither annual nor special` MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, YearMonthDay 2026 6 9, YearMonthDay 2026 6 30

#ASSERT `s 390(b) the least notice of the meeting` EQUALS `period in days` 20
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` `notice given 20 days before`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` `notice given 19 days before`
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` `notice given 21 days before`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` `notice that omits the purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` `notice sent only to the voting holders`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` `notice of a meeting that is neither annual nor special`

§ `Section 390(b) - the vote`

-- Arguments: votes in favor; the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes; a partnership with general partners?; stockholders who will become general partners; of those, how many approve.
-- "A majority of the outstanding shares": MORE than half. 51 of 100 carries; exactly 50 does not; all 100 carries; none does not.
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 50 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 100 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 0 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- counts that cannot be a vote are not covered
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 101 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 5 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` (0 MINUS 1) 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- a partnership with general partners: EACH stockholder who will become a general partner must approve as well
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 TRUE 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 50 100 TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no stockholder will become a general partner (0 of 0): nothing more is needed
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 TRUE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a partnership: the general-partner counts are not looked at
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 FALSE 2 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- counts of general partners that cannot be (more approving than there are, or negative) are not covered
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 TRUE 2 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` 51 100 TRUE (0 MINUS 1) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- one stockholder's side of the proviso: a veto only if the move is as a partnership with general partners AND the stockholder will become a general partner
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the approval of the stockholder is required for the authorization, in addition to the vote` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the approval of the stockholder is required for the authorization, in addition to the vote` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the approval of the stockholder is required for the authorization, in addition to the vote` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the approval of the stockholder is required for the authorization, in addition to the vote` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 390(b) - the certificate`

-- By position: (1) name; (2) date of the original certificate; (3) jurisdiction and resulting entity; (4) approved in accordance with the section; (5)(i) existence shall cease; (5)(ii) agreement on service of process; (6) will continue; (7) plan approved.
`a certificate of transfer certifying (1) to (5)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a certificate of transfer lacking (5)(i)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a certificate of transfer lacking (5)(ii)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a certificate of transfer lacking (3)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a certificate of continuance certifying (1) to (4) and (6)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a certificate of continuance lacking (6)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a certificate of transfer certifying (1) to (5) and (7)` MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

-- Arguments: the kind of certificate; what it certifies; a plan is adopted?
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer` `a certificate of transfer certifying (1) to (5)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer` `a certificate of transfer lacking (5)(i)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer` `a certificate of transfer lacking (5)(ii)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer` `a certificate of transfer lacking (3)` FALSE
-- a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance needs (6) and not (5)
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` `a certificate of continuance certifying (1) to (4) and (6)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` `a certificate of continuance lacking (6)` FALSE
-- (5) is not needed in a certificate of continuance; (6) is not needed in a certificate of transfer
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` `a certificate of transfer certifying (1) to (5)` FALSE
-- (7) is needed only if a plan is adopted
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer` `a certificate of transfer certifying (1) to (5)` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `a certificate of transfer` `a certificate of transfer certifying (1) to (5) and (7)` TRUE

§ `Section 390(b)(5) - service of process on the Secretary of State`

-- the registered agent's address needs the registered agent's written consent, filed with the certificate
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the address specified for the mailing of a copy of process is permitted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the address specified for the mailing of a copy of process is permitted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the address specified for the mailing of a copy of process is permitted` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the address specified for the mailing of a copy of process is permitted` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) process may be served upon the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) process may be served upon the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` FALSE
-- the letter goes to the address specified, or to the LAST address the corporation designated in writing
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the address to which the Secretary of State mails the letter notifying the corporation of the service` "1 Main Street" NOTHING EQUALS "1 Main Street"
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the address to which the Secretary of State mails the letter notifying the corporation of the service` "1 Main Street" (JUST "2 Oak Avenue") EQUALS "2 Oak Avenue"
-- the letter: mail or courier with a record of mailing or deposit, a record of delivery by signature, and the process enclosed
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the letter notifying the corporation of the service is sent as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the letter notifying the corporation of the service is sent as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the letter notifying the corporation of the service is sent as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the letter notifying the corporation of the service is sent as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- the plaintiff: in duplicate, notify the Secretary of State, pay $50
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the sum that the plaintiff pays the Secretary of State on service` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` TRUE TRUE 50
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` TRUE TRUE 49
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` TRUE TRUE 51
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` FALSE TRUE 50
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` TRUE FALSE 50
-- the $50 is taxed as costs if the plaintiff prevails; otherwise the text is silent
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the sum paid to the Secretary of State is taxed as part of the costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the sum paid to the Secretary of State is taxed as part of the costs` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the record: not required to be kept "longer than 5 years from receipt"
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the number of years from receipt of the service for which the Secretary of State must retain the record` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record of the service` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record of the service` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record of the service` 5.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record of the service` (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 390(c) - cessation`

-- Arguments: a certificate of transfer (not continuance) was filed?; all fees were paid?; the time is at or after the effective time?
#ASSERT `s 390(c) the Secretary of State must certify that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) the Secretary of State must certify that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) the Secretary of State must certify that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(c) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(c) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer, domestication or continuance out of this State` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer, domestication or continuance out of this State` FALSE

§ `Section 390(d) - what is unaffected; no winding up`

#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance leaves the matter unaffected` `an obligation or liability of the corporation incurred prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance leaves the matter unaffected` `the personal liability of a person incurred prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance leaves the matter unaffected` `the choice of law applicable to the corporation with respect to matters arising prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance leaves the matter unaffected` `another matter that the first sentence of s 390(d) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: otherwise agreed?; the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides?
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance requires the corporation to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets under this title` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance requires the corporation to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets under this title` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance requires the corporation to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets under this title` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance requires the corporation to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets under this title` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 390(e) and (f)`

#ASSERT `s 390(e) the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State, with the law of this State applying as before` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(e) the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State, with the law of this State applying as before` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(e) the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State, with the law of this State applying as before` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(e) the continuing corporation and the resulting entity constitute a single entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(e) the continuing corporation and the resulting entity constitute a single entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (f): once effective
#ASSERT `s 390(f) the resulting entity is deemed to be the same entity as the corporation, a continuation of its existence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) the resulting entity is deemed to be the same entity as the corporation, a continuation of its existence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(f) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the corporation remain vested` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the resulting entity and also the corporation, for so long as the corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State`
#ASSERT `s 390(f) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the corporation remain vested` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the resulting entity alone`
#ASSERT `s 390(f) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the corporation remain vested` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(f) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the corporation remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the resulting entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the resulting entity and also the corporation, for so long as the corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State`
#ASSERT `s 390(f) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the corporation remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the resulting entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the resulting entity alone`
#ASSERT `s 390(f) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the corporation remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the resulting entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(f) title to real property vested in the corporation reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) title to real property vested in the corporation reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(f) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the corporation are preserved unimpaired` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the corporation are preserved unimpaired` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(f) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the resulting entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the resulting entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 390(g) and (h)`

#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into cash in a transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into property in a transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the resulting entity in a transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity in a transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `cancelled in a transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `treated in a way that s 390(g) does not name` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under this section: not covered
#ASSERT `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `cancelled in a transfer, domestication or continuance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (h): no vote if no shares were issued before the board adopted the resolution
#ASSERT `s 390(h) a vote of the stockholders is necessary to authorize the transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(h) a vote of the stockholders is necessary to authorize the transfer, domestication or continuance` FALSE

§ `Section 390(i) - nonstock corporations`

#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body performs the acts required of the board of directors` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body performs the acts required of the board of directors` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body performs the acts required of the board of directors` `a charitable nonstock corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body performs the acts required of the board of directors` `a stock corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: members entitled to vote for election of the governing body?; entitled under the certificate or bylaws to vote on this or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution?; any member entitled to vote on this?; another holder of a membership interest?
#ASSERT `s 390(i) who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the members entitled to vote, and any other holder of a membership interest`
#ASSERT `s 390(i) who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the members entitled to vote, and any other holder of a membership interest`
#ASSERT `s 390(i) who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the governing body at a meeting, by a majority of its members then in office`
-- a holder of a membership interest but no member entitled to vote: not addressed
#ASSERT `s 390(i) who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the governing body's vote: a majority of the members then in office (more than half): 5 of 9 carries, 4 of 9 does not
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` 5 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` 4 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` 4 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` 5 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` 10 9 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the method and proceedings conform as nearly as may be to those prescribed by this section for corporations having capital stock` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the method and proceedings conform as nearly as may be to those prescribed by this section for corporations having capital stock` `a stock corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Attorney General: a charitable nonstock corporation only; mailed "10 days prior to the date of the proposed" transfer
#ASSERT `s 390(i) due notice must be mailed to the Attorney General` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(i) due notice must be mailed to the Attorney General` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(i) due notice must be mailed to the Attorney General` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(i) due notice must be mailed to the Attorney General` `a stock corporation`
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the least notice to the Attorney General before the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance` EQUALS `period in days` 10
-- proposed on 30 September 2026: mailed on 20 September (exactly 10 days) is in time; 21 September is not; 19 September is.
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the notice to the Attorney General was mailed in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 20) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(i) the notice to the Attorney General was mailed in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 21) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT `s 390(i) the notice to the Attorney General was mailed in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 19) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30)

§ `Section 390(j) - the plan`

#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `the terms and conditions of the transfer, domestication or continuance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `the mode of carrying the same into effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `that the governing document of the resulting entity shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock of the corporation or cancelling them, in accordance with subsection (g)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `any details or provisions as are deemed desirable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `such other provisions or facts as shall be required by the laws applicable to the resulting entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `a statement that s 390(j) does not list` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(j) a term of the plan may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` TRUE
-- the "facts" sentence: an event, and a determination or action by any person or body, are facts; a fact of another kind is not shown not to be one
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `the occurrence of any event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `a determination or action by any person or body, including the resulting entity or the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `a fact of another kind that s 390(j) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(j) a term of the plan may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` FALSE

§ `Section 390(k) - restrictions on mergers and consolidations`

#ASSERT `s 390(k) the date before which the corporation must have been incorporated, and on or before which the agreement must have been in effect` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2023 8 1
-- Arguments: where the restriction is found; date of incorporation; date the agreement came into effect; restricts a merger or consolidation?; expressly provides otherwise for a transfer, domestication or continuance?; expressly provides for a conversion?
-- a certificate of a corporation incorporated on 31 July 2023: before 1 August 2023, so (k) reaches it; deemed a merger
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a merger or consolidation`
-- incorporated ON 1 August 2023: not "before" that date
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an agreement in effect ON 1 August 2023: "on or before" that date, so (k) reaches it
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 8 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a merger or consolidation`
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 7 31) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a merger or consolidation`
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 8 2) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the provision does not restrict a merger or consolidation: not addressed
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an express provision for a transfer, domestication or continuance governs
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `as the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
-- failing that, an express provision for a conversion applies as if the transfer were a conversion
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a conversion`
-- both: the express provision for a transfer comes first ("or, if ... does not so expressly provide, a conversion")
#ASSERT `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `as the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
